v6-key-information-only-on-direct-signature.pgp:

  This certificate was generated by gosop:

    gosop generate-key --profile=security "<test@example.org>"


  The self signature on the user ID doesn't contain any information
  about the key.  Instead, the key flags, etc. are stored in the
  direct key signature.

  See https://gitlab.com/sequoia-pgp/sequoia-sq/-/issues/624
